Package: redisrs
Title: 'Redis' and 'Valkey' Client with Cluster and 'ElastiCache' Support
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Igor", "Pavlichenko", , "pawigor@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Authors of the dependency Rust crates", role = "cph",
           comment = "see LICENSE.note")
  )
Description: A client for the in-memory data stores 'Redis'
    <https://redis.io/> and 'Valkey' <https://valkey.io/>, built on the
    'Rust' library 'redis-rs' <https://github.com/redis-rs/redis-rs>.
    Connections are opened from a URL and can use network sockets, Unix
    domain sockets, Transport Layer Security (TLS) encryption, and 'Redis'
    Cluster mode, in which keys are spread over several servers. Any server
    command can be sent with arguments given as character, numeric, logical
    or raw vectors, and several commands can be sent in one network round
    trip as a pipeline. Replies are converted to R values, for example maps
    to named lists. R objects can be stored in serialized form with an
    optional expiry time and read back. For Amazon Web Services (AWS)
    'ElastiCache', the package creates Identity and Access Management (IAM)
    authentication tokens signed with the AWS Signature Version 4 method,
    and makes a new token at every connect and reconnect. A lost connection
    is reopened and the failed command is sent once more, except inside
    transactions.
